  "title": "Divin Castle",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/castle"
  ],
  "details": "<p>\"DIVIN, a castle in the Hither Circle of the Danube, in Lower Hungary, upon a very steep rock. In 1576 it was taken by the Turks, who kept it till 1593. In the year 1674, it was taken from the rebels Balassa, and demolished; so that at present it is no more than a heap of rubbish. From it a place in the neighbourhood takes its name, in whose jurisdiction it stands. The inhabitants employ themselves in agriculture and hunting.\" (Seally, 1787, Vol. 1, s.v. \u201cVidin\u201d)</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A castle built in the 13th century. Today, it is located at Devin in Slovakia's Bansk\u00e1 Bystrica region.",
